uestion_type":"application","question":"Let $K\\subseteq\\mathbb{R}^2$ be the union of the half-lines $\\{\\lambda(1,0)\\colon\\lambda\\geq0\\}$ and $\\{\\lambda(0,-1)\\colon\\lambda\\geq0\\}$, a cone that is not convex. Which set is $K^{\\circ}$?","options":["$\\{\\boldsymbol{a}\\in\\mathbb{R}^2\\colon a_1\\leq0\\text{ or }a_2\\geq0\\}$","$\\{\\boldsymbol{a}\\in\\mathbb{R}^2\\colon a_1\\leq0\\text{ and }a_2\\geq0\\}$","$\\{\\lambda(-1,0)\\colon\\lambda\\geq0\\}\\cup\\{\\lambda(0,1)\\colon\\lambda\\geq0\\}$","$\\{\\boldsymbol{a}\\in\\mathbb{R}^2\\colon a_1\\geq0\\text{ and }a_2\\leq0\\}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"0f0d03c15408634fcfbe8897","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_2_1b_math_vi_convexity_and_optimization_polar_cone_fbd18b66_011","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $\\boldsymbol{B}\\in\\mathbb{R}^{n\\times m}$ have columns $\\boldsymbol{v}_1,\\dots,\\boldsymbol{v}_m$, and let $K=\\operatorname{Cone}(\\{\\boldsymbol{v}_1,\\dots,\\boldsymbol{v}_m\\})=\\{\\boldsymbol{B}\\boldsymbol{u}\\colon\\boldsymbol{u}\\in\\mathbb{R}^m,\\ \\boldsymbol{u}\\geq\\boldsymbol{0}\\}$. Which set equals $K^{\\circ}$ for every such matrix $\\boldsymbol{B}$?","options":["$\\{\\boldsymbol{a}\\in\\mathbb{R}^m\\colon\\boldsymbol{B}\\boldsymbol{a}\\leq\\boldsymbol{0}\\}$","$\\{\\boldsymbol{B}\\boldsymbol{u}\\colon\\boldsymbol{u}\\in\\mathbb{R}^m,\\ \\boldsymbol{u}\\leq\\boldsymbol{0}\\}$","$\\{\\boldsymbol{a}\\in\\mathbb{R}^n\\colon\\boldsymbol{a}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{B}\\boldsymbol{u}\\leq0\\text{ for some }\\boldsymbol{u}\\geq\\boldsymbol{0},\\ \\boldsymbol{u}\\neq\\boldsymbol{0}\\}$","$\\{\\boldsymbol{a}\\in\\mathbb{R}^n\\colon\\boldsymbol{B}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{a}\\leq\\boldsymbol{0}\\}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"b150b12e899c0bc976a05f07","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_2_1b_math_vi_convexity_and_optimization_polar_cone_fbd18b66_012","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $K\\subseteq\\mathbb{