d974","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_2_1b_math_vi_convexity_and_optimization_polar_cone_fbd18b66_018","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Two cones $K_1\\subseteq K_2$ in $\\mathbb{R}^n$ have the same polar cone, $K_1^{\\circ}=K_2^{\\circ}$. Which conclusion holds for every such pair?","options":["The two cones coincide: $K_1=K_2$.","The larger cone satisfies $K_2\\subseteq(K_1^{\\circ})^{\\circ}$.","The two cones have the same closure: $\\operatorname{Cl}(K_1)=\\operatorname{Cl}(K_2)$.","$K_2$ is the smallest convex cone that contains $K_1$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"0a085fbdb2f2312313279a4a","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_2_1b_math_vi_convexity_and_optimization_polar_cone_fbd18b66_019","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"Let $K=\\{\\boldsymbol{x}\\in\\mathbb{R}^2\\colon x_1>0,\\ x_2>0\\}\\cup\\{\\boldsymbol{0}\\}$, a convex cone that is not closed. Which set is its polar cone $K^{\\circ}$?","options":["$\\{\\boldsymbol{a}\\in\\mathbb{R}^2\\colon a_1<0,\\ a_2<0\\}\\cup\\{\\boldsymbol{0}\\}$","$\\{\\boldsymbol{a}\\in\\mathbb{R}^2\\colon a_1+a_2\\leq0\\}$","$\\{\\boldsymbol{a}\\in\\mathbb{R}^2\\colon a_1\\leq0,\\ a_2\\leq0\\}$","$\\{\\boldsymbol{a}\\in\\mathbb{R}^2\\colon a_1\\geq0,\\ a_2\\geq0\\}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"bb08413ddacce65afa54f64e","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_2_1b_math_vi_convexity_and_optimization_polar_cone_fbd18b66_020","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"Let $K=\\operatorname{Cone}(\\{(1,0,0),(0,1,0),(-1,-1,0)\\})\\subseteq\\mathbb{R}^3$. Which set is its polar cone $K^{\\circ}$?","options":["The line $\\{(0,0,\\mu)\\colon\\mu\\in\\mathbb{R}\\}$","The zero cone $\\{\\boldsymbol{0}\\}$","The half-line $\\{(0,0,\\mu)\\colon\\mu\\geq0\\}$","The set $\\{\\boldsymbol{a}\\in\\mathbb{R}^3\\colon a_1\\leq0,\\ a_2\\leq0\\}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"0b84e0e9f77a879d1ac77b62","time_limit":40}]}}